// Was SOUNDNESS QUEUE row self_literal_local_borrow_pins_impl_region_admits; closed 2026-09-23: a literal whose type names an impl lifetime (`Self` in `impl<'s>`) takes that region, so a local borrow must live for all of it.
// ADMISSION, tier 2 — Rust refuses (E0597), logosc compiles. Inside `impl<'s> Foo<'s>`,
// `Self { r: &v }` IS `Foo<'s>`: the literal pins the impl's region, `'s` outlives the
// function, and `v` is a body local — "`v` does not live long enough" even though the
// value never escapes. logosc types a literal from its values and never meets `'s`.
// NEIGHBOUR of nllmoves.R13 (issue-98170), ROWED WITH REASON (2) DOORS IN SERIES, measured
// 2026-09-13a-selfregion on build 20b6d3c2a8770cbf: under `selfv` (body Self carries the
// header's regions + the checked Self literal + named header binders) the literal check is
// LIVE and PASSES — census `selflitv.site 2`, `selflitv.override 2`, `selflitv.differs 2`,
// still compiles — because `&v`'s region is EMPTY at the literal, and an empty region is
// permissive in the variance check. The door that gives a local borrow a region (12q's door L,
// declined on four legal refusals) must open first.
package self_literal_local_borrow_pins_impl_region_fail;
struct Foo<'s> { r: &'s i64 }
impl<'s> Foo<'s> {
    fn peek(self: &Self) -> i64 {
        let v: i64 = 40i64;
        let t = Self { r: &v };
        return *t.r;
    }
}
fn main() -> i32 {
    let w: i64 = 1i64;
    let f = Foo { r: &w };
    return f.peek() as i32;
}
